			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I currently rely on Netlify Forms, so I’d have to find an alternative for a contact form on one site. It only gets like… one hit per month, maybe, so if things were really desperate I’d make a new email account and put up a mailto link until I found an alternative provider.</p><p>The harder thing to change than hosting provider would be if I needed to replace GitHub, due to the integrations and widespread support.</p><p>That said, I’m primarily building static sites. Backends add complexity.</p>",
